	<br><div id='review' style='margin: auto;'><div class='review-BL-top'><!-- empty --></div><div class='review-BL-mid'><div style='padding: 3px 0 3px 5px; border-bottom: 2px solid #38719C; text-align: left; margin: 0px 5px;'><img src = 'images/circle.gif'><a href = '/index.php?page=detailedlistserver&serid=23556&url_sname=SpringRO' class='sb_m' >
		SpringRO - 1x/1x/1x</a></div><div style='padding: 2px; border-bottom: 2px solid #38719C; margin: 0px 5px;'>
		<table cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>
			<tr class='switch'>
				<td width=140> &nbsp; <a href = 'index.php?page=userprofile&uid=82313' class = 'rev_sw' >Poofy</a></td>
				<td width=115><div style='width: 91; height: 20; background: url(images/overall.gif) repeat-x 0 0;'><!-- empty --></div></td>
				<td width=180 align='center'>Played for 1 month</td>
				<td width=70 align='right'>2026-11-01</td>
			</tr>
		</table>
	</div><div class='btext_mm' style='padding: 2px; overflow: auto; width:510; word-wrap:break-word; margin: 0px 8px;'>Big pull is implemented RetroAchievements if your thing. Many cool custom class tweaks but some are odd (Why buff archers?) Server had brief DDoS and host issues that seem on track to be resolved, will update score if holds. GMs can be helpful enough but weirdly abrasive? Allowing suggestions through Discord, seeing one get shut down due to wanting to focus on catering to &quot;the 80% and not the 20%&quot; of players only to lock it when it generates discussion and popularity is certainly off-putting.</div><div id='revinfo' style='height: 16px;'>
		<div style='width:150px; float:left;'>			
